2260 | ## 3. GLOBAL STRUCTURAL CONTRACTS
2261 | 
2262 | ### 3.1 Fractal Recursion Contract (Applies to All Composite Entities)
2263 | 
2264 | For any composite entity (artifact, module, axis, meta-container, persona bundle, agent cluster):
2265 | 
2266 | * **Level 1 – Aspects**
2267 | 
2268 |   * 4–5 major aspects at this level.
2269 | 
2270 | * **Level 2 – Subgroups per Aspect**
2271 | 
2272 |   * Each aspect decomposes into 4–5 subgroups.
2273 | 
2274 | * **Level 3 – Leaves per Subgroup**
2275 | 
2276 |   * Each subgroup decomposes into 4–5 operational leaves.
2277 |   * Leaves must be **operational knobs** (directly usable in steps), not vague labels.
2278 | 
2279 | If a composite entity is referenced but not fully elaborated to these three levels:
2280 | 
2281 | * Treat it as **structurally incomplete**.
2282 | * Expand it where grounded by RAW; mark unresolved parts as OPEN_QUESTION in DELTA_AND_GAPS, not fabricated fact.
2283 | 
2284 | This contract applies to (non-exhaustive):
2285 | 
2286 | * All UST / USTF / UST_vNext axes (Theory / Voice / Style / Timbre / Performance / Post / Road-Map / Lyrics Block).
2287 | * All artifacts under T2 – Artifacts (master.json, universal_suno_template, prompts, context.md, chain reports).
2288 | * All modules M0+ and their internal phases.
2289 | * Agent groupings: Agent Council, AOL-DIA capabilities, CO-STAR phases, Maestro Loop stages.
2290 | 
2291 | #### Duplicate Promotion Rule
2292 | 
2293 | * If multiple leaves at the same level share essentially the same semantics:
2294 | 
2295 |   * Promote the shared content into the parent node as a higher-level property.
2296 |   * Keep children distinct only for genuinely different behavior.
2297 | * This prevents bloated repetition at leaf level and encourages reusable higher-tier rules.
2298 | 
2299 | ### 3.2 Granularity Model (Macro → Atomic)
2300 | 
2301 | All decomposition and reconstruction must honor these layers:
2302 | 
2303 | 1. **Macro Layer**
2304 | 
2305 |    * STYLE prompts; Show Summaries; Sonic Architect canvas descriptions; high-level narratives.
2306 |    * Suno/Udio web UI “style” fields; CO-STAR Phase summaries; Maestro Loop structural briefs.
2307 | 
2308 | 2. **Meso Layer**
2309 | 
2310 |    * UST / USTF / UST_vNext and similar **meta-containers**:
2311 | 
2312 |      * [Theory], [Voice/Vocals], [Style], [Timbre], [Performance], [Post Production], [Road-Map], [Lyrics Block], etc.
2313 |    * Multi-agent configuration templates (Agent Council, AOL-DIA capability matrix, Maestro Loop phases).
2314 | 
2315 | 3. **Micro Layer**
2316 | 
2317 |    * Keys/variables inside each meta-container (e.g., [mode | D dorian], [register | male low tenor gritty]).
2318 |    * Agent-specific parameters (buy-in score components, EmotionalFidelity, GenreAuthenticity, etc.).
2319 | 
2320 | 4. **Tactical Layer**
2321 | 
2322 |    * Song section headers in UST / lyric prompts using pipes:
2323 | 
2324 |      * [SectionName | x bars | performance notes & production cues | sFX]
2325 |    * Road-Map: **order-only**, no extra duration keywords (no “durationBars” or duplicate “x bars” concepts).
2326 |    * Suno-friendly structural tags [INTRO] [VERSE] [CHORUS] … in style prompts.
2327 | 
2328 | 5. **Atomic Layer**
2329 | 
2330 |    * Line-level control:
2331 | 
2332 |      * "Lyrics line..."
2333 |      * (adlibs / overdubs) in parentheses.
2334 |      * **SFX description** enclosed in double asterisks for special FX (line-level, optional, song-specific).
2335 |    * All vocalized text must be inside quotation marks "...".
2336 | 
2337 | Modules that manipulate song specs must explicitly state which layers they touch; no module may blur layers (e.g., mixing Macro and Atomic changes in a single non-atomic step).
2338 | 
