3086 | SECTION 3 — MODULE_SEQUENCE_ATOMIC
3087 | M0_session_init_and_state_load
3088 | Purpose: Initialize environment and ingest all primary inputs into RAW state.
3089 | Inputs: T1_Inputs
3090 | Outputs: S_raw_corpus, S_rule_registry, S_change_request_log, S_session_ledger
3091 | Steps:
3092 | M0.1 Initialize runtime containers
3093 | M0.1.1 Create S_raw_corpus (empty list)
3094 | M0.1.2 Create S_rule_registry (empty map)
3095 | M0.1.3 Create S_change_request_log (empty list)
3096 | M0.2 Ingest conversation + files
3097 | M0.2.1 For each input file/chunk, append to S_raw_corpus with source_tag and timestamp
3098 | M0.2.2 Detect embedded monoliths and tag as T2 artifacts
3099 | M0.3 Initialize version counters and identifiers
3100 | M0.3.1 seed session_id, CR_counter, ledger_seq
3101 | 
3102 | M1_change_request_handler
3103 | Purpose: Normalize new human messages into CRs and update registry.
3104 | Inputs: S_raw_corpus, new_message
3105 | Outputs: S_rule_registry, S_change_request_log
3106 | Steps:
3107 | M1.1 Detect rule-like language (pattern match: "must","never","from now on","correction")
