4910 | 5 Whys (root-cause chain)
4911 | 
4912 | Why ingest input? → To create a canonical source (S_raw_corpus) for all processing.
4913 | 
4914 | Why need a canonical source? → To preserve provenance and enable reproducible runs.
4915 | 
4916 | Why is provenance important? → To audit decisions, validate remediation, and trace CRs.
4917 | 
4918 | Why must runs be auditable? → Because governance rules require lineage and non-destructive edits.
4919 | 
4920 | Why require non-destructive edits? → To prevent loss of original IP and support reversible remediation.
4921 | 
4922 | M1 — M1_change_request_handler
4923 | Definition: Detects human Change Requests (CRs), registers rule updates, and marks supersession relationships in S_rule_registry.
