4935 | 
4936 | How: Pattern-match CR tokens, create cr_id objects, compare vs existing rules, persist supersession links.
4937 | 
4938 | 5 Whys
4939 | 
4940 | Why capture CRs? → To convert informal edits into enforceable rules.
4941 | 
4942 | Why convert edits? → To ensure system behavior aligns with the user’s latest intent.
4943 | 
4944 | Why enforce latest intent? → To maintain deterministic outputs across runs.
4945 | 
4946 | Why demand determinism? → To enable reproducible pipelines and reliable downstream automation.
4947 | 
4948 | Why is reliability required? → For auditability, co-development, and IP portability.
