5469 | F — Operational rules / prompts to ensure a new session “knows” them
5470 | Include this short instruction near top of your zero-touch prompt (M11 output) so any fresh GPT or session model will process SEG/G-Card correctly:
5471 | 
5472 | Require schema versions: SEG.schema_version == "1.0" and G_CARD.schema_version == "1.0". If missing, compute SEG and produce G_CARD.
5473 | 
5474 | Enforce detection keys: look for seg, g_card, [[SEG:BEGIN]], [[G-CARD:BEGIN]]. Exact key matching only.
5475 | 
5476 | Enforce pass threshold: if seg.composite_pct >= 97.5 and all gates true => final_decision = PASS. Else: CONDITIONAL (if single small deficiencies) or HOLD (if major gates fail).
5477 | 
5478 | Always attach ledger pointers: ledger_pointers must include __raw_chunk_index references for traceability.
5479 | 
5480 | Output: always serialize both SEG and G_CARD JSON objects into the chain report and context.md.
